I'm building an app that will allow a business owner whose business is about
lending, collection and repayment of money to & from customers through various
Account Managers who have an average of 200 customers each and do daily/
weekly collection & repayment. I want a simple yet robust application or solution
that will allow the business owner to monitor transactions in real time (after input
from account managers or credit alerts from the Bank) to provide accurate daily
balances across the loaning, collection, and repayment sides. Kindly assist with a
well-structured brief write-up on this, with a well-defined architectural design for
such a solution and how to achieve this in the shortest possible time.
Proposed Solution: Loan, Collection & Repayment
Management System
1. Business Objective
The proposed solution will provide a centralized platform for managing and monitoring the
complete lending and collection lifecycle.
It will enable the business owner to:
Register and manage customers.
Assign customers to Account Managers.
Create and manage loans.
Track daily/weekly repayment schedules.
Record collections made by Account Managers.
Capture bank credit alerts automatically where bank integration is available.
Reconcile Account Manager collections against bank deposits.
Monitor outstanding loans and customer balances.
Track Account Manager performance.
View real-time financial positions.
Generate daily, weekly and monthly reports.
Detect discrepancies, overdue repayments and unaccounted collections.
With approximately 200 customers per Account Manager, the system should be
designed around customer → loan → repayment schedule → transaction → ledger
relationships.
